  "details": "- CVE-2026-81634: bounds-check the scratch buffer in rrset_canonical() and\n  rrset_canonicalize_to_buffer() before writing the RRSIG rdata, the first\n  canonical owner name and each RR's rdata, so a large rrset can no longer\n  be written past the end of the buffer\n- CVE-2026-80225: cap the number of pipelined TCP/DoT queries drained per\n  event-loop visit in tcp_req_info_read_again() and tcp_more_read_again()\n  and defer the remainder via a zero-delay timer, so one connection can no\n  longer starve the other file descriptors",
